course: dictionary
lesson: 6398
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a serious meaning and a light, everyday meaning. Murder is one of them. Its main meaning is a very serious crime: killing a person on purpose, which is against the law. Detectives in mystery stories solve this kind of puzzle.
explain: History books use the word in its serious sense too. «The Nazis murdered about six million Jews» shows how terrible this crime was. You will learn more about it when you are older.
explain: In everyday talk, especially in the UK and Ireland, murder can mean something very hard or unpleasant, or wanting something very much. Check the clues: «The traffic was murder today» means it was very hard to get anywhere, not that anyone was hurt.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. Ask what the sentence is about. A crime story means the serious meaning. A cup of tea or a busy road means the everyday meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Murder» as a verb means to kill a person on purpose, against the law.
fact: «Murder» can also mean something very hard or unpleasant, as in «The traffic was murder».
fact: «Could murder» means you want something very much, as in «I could murder a cup of tea».
fact: «Get away with murder» means doing bad things and not being punished.
exercise: «The traffic was murder today.» What does murder mean here? | A crime against the law | *Something very hard or unpleasant | Very quiet | A kind of song
exercise: «She murdered that song.» What does murdered suggest? | She sang it brilliantly | *She did it very badly | She stopped singing | She wrote the song in a crime story
exercise: Which word means to want something very much? | Traffic | Whisper | *Murder | Today
test: «I could murder a cup of tea.» What does could murder mean here? | *Really want | Really hate the tea | Really dislike | Really sell
test: In a mystery story, what is the murder? | A happy party | *The puzzle the detectives solve | A long walk in the rain | A map of the town
exam: Which meaning of murder is a serious crime? | Something very hard | *To kill a person on purpose, against the law | To want something very much | To do something badly
